\newlabel{fig:ood}{{5}{13}{Two-axis OOD separation. Blue: 20 trained languages (ratio $\ge 5\times $, absolute ppl $\le 6.5$). Diamonds: 6 unseen — byte-adjacent (lv, ga) collapse on the ratio axis; cross-script (zh, ja, hi, iu) sit orders above on the absolute axis. hi breaches the trained ratio floor (5.74$\times $): the one-axis rule fails informatively; both axes together separate all 26}{figure.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Cross-script routing on the fixed-regime chain (40 crops per probe). zh 37/40, ja 40/40, hi 40/40 and the decontaminated iu 40/40 concentrate on the only two territories with substantial multi-byte training exposure (bg/el: 82\% 2-byte characters vs 11.7\% next-highest); no Latin-route attraction remains after the iu correction. No linguistic kinship exists between any probe and Cyrillic or Greek.}}{14}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:xscript}{{6}{14}{Cross-script routing on the fixed-regime chain (40 crops per probe). zh 37/40, ja 40/40, hi 40/40 and the decontaminated iu 40/40 concentrate on the only two territories with substantial multi-byte training exposure (bg/el: 82\% 2-byte characters vs 11.7\% next-highest); no Latin-route attraction remains after the iu correction. No linguistic kinship exists between any probe and Cyrillic or Greek}{figure.6}{}}
